courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon completion of this course, students are expected to be able to:

1. understand the conceptual framework, aims and objectives of General Studies, and its position in the primary curriculum;
2. use appropriate teaching strategies and methods for the subject;
3. implement the integrated curriculum through effective application of the interdisciplinary approach;
4. design and implement various modes of assessment for General Studies;
5. deliver GS lessons effectively;
6. possess the awareness to be reflective for future professional development.

